From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 21:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: add transactional dual-VLAN DSA offload

Extend the Qualcomm PPE ingress and egress translation paths to match
and modify SVID and CVID independently. This lets the RTL837x 802.1ad
source-port tag coexist with one ordinary customer VLAN while keeping
the QCA4B and direct-PHY paths unchanged.

Treat QinQ port roles as shared transactional state. Ingress VLAN
topologies hold both role directions, while destination-only RTL flows
hold only egress. Roll roles and every partially programmed table back
in reverse order, and restore edge mode after the final owner leaves.

Only request VLAN actions for tag slots which are actually present.
Use the QSDK ADD_OR_REPLACE egress semantics and match all tag formats
so stripped routed packets and software-tagged control packets share a
deterministic restoration path. Keep valid DSA MAC addresses while
walking PPPoE paths and expose topology failures, VLAN slots and role
references for runtime diagnosis.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_bridge.c
